course: dictionary
lesson: 5544
title: Clear enough to read
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how well writing can be read. «Make your handwriting legible.» The teacher wants your writing to be clear enough to read easily, so legible must mean just that.
explain: Look at the words around legible for clues. Handwriting is what needs to be read, and «Signs and labels must be legible.» A sign has to be easy to read at a glance, so legible must mean clear and easy to read.
explain: Legible is about writing or print. A messy scribble that nobody can read is not legible. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "Make your handwriting clear enough to read easily." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Legible means clear enough to be read easily.
fact: Legible is an adjective, and its adverb is legibly, which means in a way that can be read easily.
fact: Legible describes writing or print, such as handwriting, signs and labels.
fact: The opposite is illegible, which means too messy or faint to read.
fact: In a test, writing the marker cannot read cannot get a mark.
exercise: «Make your handwriting legible.» What does legible mean? | Very loud | Neatly folded | Written in pencil | *Clear enough to be read easily
exercise: «Signs and labels must be legible.» Why must a sign be legible? | So it is very heavy | So it can be hidden from view | *So people can read it easily | So it can be painted in bright colours
exercise: «The marker wrote, Your answer is not legible.» Find and copy the word that means clear enough to read easily. | answer | wrote | marker | *legible
test: In a test, the marker cannot read your answer. Why might you lose the mark? | You used a long word | Your pencil is sharp | You wrote on the back of the page | *Your writing is not legible
test: Which word is the adverb form of legible? | legibility | legal | *legibly | legible
exam: Mia's label on the jar is smudged and faint. Is it legible? | *No, it is not clear enough to be read easily | Yes, it is very loud | Yes, because it is written in pencil | No, because it is too short
